      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T21:06:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Now that we are adding a 3rd out parameter, I think we should probably just define a simple struct in this header that is \n\n    struct FragSkSL {\n         std::string fSkSL;\n         BlendInfo fBlendInfo;\n         bool fRequiresLocalCoords;\n         int fNumTexturesAndSamplers\n    }; // or some related name\n    \nThen GetSkSLFS can simply return all of this metadata with the sksl. This is not a perf hotspot so having it return a larger type vs. filling out existing stack variables doesn\u0027t seem critical and will help simplify the function signature.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "f9be2773fa2e2b63b04a7c5f7b2a82db253b61c6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf1809fa_1692517e",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T21:19:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1. Though I\u0027m also wondering if DawnGraphicsPipeline could just query the RenderStep(s) directly to build the bind group layout from structured data instead of having to go through ContextUtils helpers. One blocker in that way is the way `RenderStep::texturesAndSamplersSkSL` works today as Michael commented on elsewhere.",
      "parentUuid": "22c85e29_188e1bc2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "f9be2773fa2e2b63b04a7c5f7b2a82db253b61c6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57740cc5_fe50ecd1",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T08:06:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could change `RenderStep` to return structured data to help `DawnGraphicsPipeline` extract number of textures directly to build bind group layout. However, I think that is a bit redundant on `DawnGraphicsPipeline` side to do the calculation after `GetSkSLFS` call. Because in that case `DawnGraphicsPipeline` would also have to manually loop through the PainParams\u0027 corresponding shader blocks to calculate total number of textures, similar to what `ShaderInfo::toSkSL` is doing afaik.\n\nSo imo, it\u0027s better to just do two things in one step: `ShaderInfo::toSkSL` does both the SkSL generation and reflections/total number of textures\u0027 computation in one pass.",
      "parentUuid": "cf1809fa_1692517e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "f9be2773fa2e2b63b04a7c5f7b2a82db253b61c6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bc7f4854_af44a6f1",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Renderer.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T21:06:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Skia follows this pattern in several places, but it\u0027s the first use of it in RenderStep, where other reflection of its shading programs are just available as values. \n\nI don\u0027t know if Graphite has enough types yet to be able to adequately let RenderStep just have an array of samplers that it exposes, and then the logic in `texturesAndSamplersSkSL` goes away entirely because it\u0027s just auto generated, and the program builder can immediately know how many textures and samplers it uses.\n\nCC\u0027ing Jim, who first added these functions to weigh in on it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "f9be2773fa2e2b63b04a7c5f7b2a82db253b61c6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "451b022f_624fc7bf",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Renderer.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T21:19:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was going to leave a comment here along the same lines. If RenderSteps could return a structured description of its texture/sampler binding declarations (similarly to how things work for attribute declarations today), it would be easier to extract that information to build the bind group layout.",
      "parentUuid": "bc7f4854_af44a6f1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "f9be2773fa2e2b63b04a7c5f7b2a82db253b61c6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bde9f353_7f610fc8",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Renderer.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T08:06:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we want to return structured data (e.g array of texture\u0027s descriptions) instead of the SkSL code here, what should be included in the descriptions?\n\nCurrently I don\u0027t see anything useful besides strings array of textures\u0027 names. If we expose more than that (filtering, tile mode, etc), then the logic of `writeUniformsAndTextures` function would be moved to the caller instead (because now there would be enough info for the caller to do that directly). In that case, there would be too many changes need to be done in this CL. Perhaps we could do this in another CL?",
      "parentUuid": "451b022f_624fc7bf",
